---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import AtlasFilter from '../../components/AtlasFilter';
import Status from '../../components/Status.astro';
import { release, url } from '../../lib/publication';
const visible = release.observations.filter(o => Number.isFinite(o.value) && release.sources.some(s => s.id === o.sourceId) && release.claims.some(c => c.id === o.claimId && ['verified','attributed','corrected'].includes(c.status)));
const local = release.geographies.filter(g => ['state','union_territory','ut'].includes(g.type));
const latestRainfall = visible.filter(o => o.metricId === 'rainfall_departure_pct').reduce((latest, row) => row.periodEnd > latest ? row.periodEnd : latest, '').slice(0, 10);
const cwcSource = release.sources.find(s => s.id === 'E-CWC-RSMS-20260910');
---
<Site title="Explore the evidence"><PageHeader title="Explore what we know" eyebrow="Evidence atlas" description={`${visible.length} approved observations; ${local.length} state and union territory coverage records. Select a place to see what is measured, what is still unknown, and the original evidence.`} />
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><Status compact /><div class="atlas-coverage" role="group" aria-label="Snapshot coverage"><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Measured rainfall</p><strong>{visible.filter(o => o.metricId === 'rainfall_departure_pct').length}</strong><p>India and broad IMD regions. Latest approved cutoff date: {latestRainfall || 'unrecorded'}; clock hour unspecified.</p></div><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Monitored storage</p><strong>{visible.filter(o => o.metricId === 'reservoir_live_storage_bcm').length}</strong><p>CWC reservoir cohorts, with their own status date and source. Not a basin or local supply value.</p></div><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Local directory</p><strong>{local.length}</strong><p>State and UT records. {local.filter(g => visible.some(o => o.geographyId === g.id)).length} have approved local numeric observations.</p></div></div><p class="small muted">Counts describe this publication’s reviewed coverage, not national monitoring coverage. District, basin flow, groundwater and household service layers remain unmeasured here. The Places layer offers an explicitly schematic locator without boundary geometry or measured state shading.</p><a class="atlas-place-entry" href="?view=coverage#atlas-workbench">Open the 36-place schematic locator <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Investigate · three evidence layers</p><h2>Move through the story</h2></div><p>Tap the bars, gauges and schematic place tiles. Every selection carries its source and date; the URL can be shared.</p></div><AtlasFilter client:load geographies={release.geographies} observations={visible} claims={release.claims} sourceBase={url('/sources/')} stateBase={url('/states/')} /><noscript><div class="note"><strong>Interactive layer controls need JavaScript.</strong><p>The rainfall records and source links above remain readable. For the other layers, read the <a href={url('/basins/')}>CWC monitored storage explanation</a>{cwcSource && <> and <a href={url(`/sources/${cwcSource.id}/`)}>its exact bulletin record</a></>}, or browse the <a href={url('/states/')}>state and union territory directory</a>. Missing local values remain unknown.</p></div></noscript></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Read across layers</p><h2>What these pictures do—and do not—connect</h2></div></div><div class="grid-3"><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Rain is an input</h3><p>IMD’s reported departure compares accumulated rainfall with a historical normal for the same dates. It does not say how much usable water is stored or delivered.</p><a href={url('/understand/rainfall-departure/')}>Understand the denominator ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Storage is a monitored cohort</h3><p>CWC’s live-storage volumes cover 178 selected reservoirs and a 50-reservoir southern subset on 10 September. They are neither a complete national inventory nor household supply.</p><a href={url('/basins/')}>Trace the basin questions ↗</a></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3>Place needs its own proof</h3><p>The state and UT tiles show where this publication has local numeric evidence. The Karnataka declaration is a separate official action, not a substitute for observed water conditions.</p><a href={url('/states/')}>Open the place directory ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">What the map cannot say yet</p><h2>Follow the geography</h2></div><p>Administrative, meteorological and catchment boundaries answer different questions.</p></div><div class="grid-3"><article class="editorial-card"><h3><a class="title-link" href={url('/states/')}>States & UTs ↗</a></h3><p>Find an official roster entry and the exact local coverage status. Regional IMD values are never copied into a state.</p></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3><a class="title-link" href={url('/districts/')}>District evidence ↗</a></h3><p>See why matching administrative codes, dates and source footprints is required before localizing a number.</p></article><article class="editorial-card"><h3><a class="title-link" href={url('/basins/')}>Basins & flows ↗</a></h3><p>Trace how a watershed, storage system and service network would be checked, without inventing a flow map.</p></article></div></div></section></Site>
